</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>VERITAS: A Four-Stage Pipeline for Data Critique and Refinement</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To move beyond a single-critic setting, VERITAS decomposes data curation into four successive stages, each adding an orthogonal source of reliability. Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ VERITAS: Leveraging Vision Priors and Expert Fusion to Improve Multimodal Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> gives an overview.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 1: Vision-Prior Extraction</span> We first ground every sample with explicit perceptual evidence. Two off-the-shelf specialist models are invoked on the input image <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.E1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Tags</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{RAM^{++}}(I)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>RAM</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{RAM^{++}}(I),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.E2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">OCR</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{PP\text{-}OCRv4}(I)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>PP</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>OCRv4</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{PP\text{-}OCRv4}(I).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The resulting object labels and text strings are serialised as a string prior
<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\{\text{Tags},\text{OCR}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>Tags</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>OCR</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\{\text{Tags},\text{OCR}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and appended to all subsequent prompts using a natural-language wrapper.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 2: Tri-Expert Assessment with Shrinkage Fusion</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Multi-Expert Critique.</span> Three state-of-the-art MLLMs (GPT-4o, Gemini-2.5-Pro, and Doubao-1.5-pro) independently assess answer quality, with each model <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> producing:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{m},r_{m})=\mathcal{M}^{(m)}_{\text{critic}}(I,q,a_{0},V\mid\mathcal{E}_{c})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>critic</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{m},r_{m})=\mathcal{M}^{(m)}_{\text{critic}}(I,q,a_{0},V\mid\mathcal{E}_{c})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}\in[0,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}\in[0,5]</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar score and <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is a structured rationale following our evaluation rubric <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each expert receives the same vision priors extracted in Stage 1, ensuring grounded assessments.(The complete prompt template is shown in Appendix <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>)</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Domain-Aware Score Fusion.</span> Three MLLMs produce raw scores <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}(n)\in[0,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}(n)\in[0,5]</annotation></semantics></math>. We transform them into a single confidence <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{S}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{S}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> through the following steps.
(1) z-normalise each critic inside its domain;
(2) compute a domain-wise signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) and use it as a weight;
(3) shrink that weight toward a corpus prior via an empirical-Bayes factor <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{d}=N_{d}/(N_{d}+\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{d}=N_{d}/(N_{d}+\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>;
(4) form the weighted average of the normalised scores;
(5) map the result back to the 0–5 rubric by a robust 5 %–95 % percentile stretch. The specific process is presented in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 3.2 VERITAS: A Four-Stage Pipeline for Data Critique and Refinement ‣ 3 Method ‣ VERITAS: Leveraging Vision Priors and Expert Fusion to Improve Multimodal Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 3: Integration with GRPO Critic</span> We distil fused judgement Ŝ into a 7B parameter critic using <em id="S3.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Group Relative Policy Optimisation</em> (GRPO). GRPO eliminates an extra value–function by comparing the candidate answer with a <span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">group baseline</span> drawn from the same old policy, thereby producing a low-variance, self-normalising advantage.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Training objective.</span>
For every image–question pair <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, we sample a group of <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> drafts <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math> from the policy <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The new policy <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated by maximising</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)={}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)={}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q,\{o_{i}\}}\,\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\Biggl[" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q,\{o_{i}\}}\,\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\Biggl[</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min\Bigl(\dfrac{\pi_{\theta}^{i,t}}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}^{i,t}}\hat{A}_{i,t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min\Bigl(\dfrac{\pi_{\theta}^{i,t}}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}^{i,t}}\hat{A}_{i,t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{clip}\bigl(\dfrac{\pi_{\theta}^{i,t}}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}^{i,t}},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\bigr)\hat{A}_{i,t}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{clip}\bigl(\dfrac{\pi_{\theta}^{i,t}}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}^{i,t}},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\bigr)\hat{A}_{i,t}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E4Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\beta\,\mathrm{D}_{\text{KL}}\bigl(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\text{ref}}\bigr)\Biggr]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\beta\,\mathrm{D}_{\text{KL}}\bigl(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\text{ref}}\bigr)\Biggr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the group–relative advantage</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reward design.</span> Each rollout receives two additive rewards
<math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}=R_{\text{acc}}+R_{\text{fmt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>fmt</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}=R_{\text{acc}}+R_{\text{fmt}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">•Accuracy reward (<math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{acc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{acc}}</annotation></semantics></math>) compares the scalar score extracted from <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with the Stage-2 “gold” <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{S}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{acc}}=\max\!\Bigl(0,1-\frac{|\text{int}(o_{i})-\hat{S}|}{5}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>int</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{acc}}=\max\!\Bigl(0,1-\frac{|\text{int}(o_{i})-\hat{S}|}{5}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">•Format reward (<math id="S3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{fmt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>fmt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{fmt}}</annotation></semantics></math>) encourages the critic style we need downstream:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\#\bigl(\texttt{&lt;Question Analysis&gt;}\in o_{i}\bigr)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;Question Analysis&gt;</mtext><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\#\bigl(\texttt{&lt;Question Analysis&gt;}\in o_{i}\bigr)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\#\bigl(\texttt{&lt;Evaluation Reasons&gt;}\in o_{i}\bigr)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;Evaluation Reasons&gt;</mtext><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\#\bigl(\texttt{&lt;Evaluation Reasons&gt;}\in o_{i}\bigr)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E6Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\#\bigl(\texttt{&lt;Scoring&gt;}\in o_{i}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;Scoring&gt;</mtext><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\#\bigl(\texttt{&lt;Scoring&gt;}\in o_{i}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{fmt}}=0.5\times\left(\dfrac{N}{3}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>fmt</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{fmt}}=0.5\times\left(\dfrac{N}{3}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The indicator function <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\#\bigl(s_{k}\in o_{i}\bigl)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#\bigl(s_{k}\in o_{i}\bigl)</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> appears in <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Domain-Aware Expert Score Fusion</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">input :</span> Scores <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1..3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1..3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1..3</annotation></semantics></math>; domain labels <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(n)</annotation></semantics></math>; constants <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=100</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">output :</span> Fused confidence <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{S}(n)\in[0,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{S}(n)\in[0,5]</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 0: domain statistics</span>
<span id="algorithm1.4.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.3.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leftarrow 1\textbf{ to }3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold"> to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leftarrow 1\textbf{ to }3</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
